# HIGH LEVEL OVERVIEW

We want to create a word-level tokenizer that tokenizes the following text:

paragraphs = [
    "In 2026, we teach `intro-to-AI` with hands-on labs—no hype. Students ask: `Why tokens?` Because models read pieces, not words. E.g., `ChatGPT-5` ≠ `Chat`, `GPT`, `5` in all schemes. We track loss/accuracy, compare char/word/BPE, and test a URL: https://example.org/a/b?c=42. Café prices rose 3.7%—blame supply-chain weirdness (and ☕ demand).",
]

# PSEUDECODE STEP BY STEP

1) Convert the Text
text_lowercase = make “paragraphs” lowercase
text_clean = remove punctuation & replace all characters that is not a letter, digit or whitespace with a space in “text_lowercase”
words = split “text_clean” by whitespaces, keeping duplicate words
print: len of words to see the total word count of the paragraph (incl. duplicate words)
tokens = split “text_lowercase” by whitespaces, removing duplicate words
print: len of tokens to see number of different words in var tokens

2)Create a Vocabulary
vocabulary = dictionary of sorted unique tokens/words
stoi = for every word w in vocabulary, enumerate it 
itos = for every number in stoi, convert back into word of the vocabulary
vocabulary_size = len of vocabulary
    
print vocabulary: print items of individual words in dictionary
print vocabulary_size: print number of different words

3)Encode Tokens into IDs
encoded_tokens = for each word in tokens, get the associated ID from stoic & form a list
print: encoded_tokens

4)Decode IDs into Tokens
decoded_token = for every ID in itos, get the associated word & form a list
print: decoded_tokens

5)Generate 5-Word Sentence
sentence = glue 5 words of decoded_tokens together with a space in between each word 
print: sentence
